{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses, Pharaoh will not listen to you</b> — because it was fitting that Pharaoh and his servants would be terrified by the plague of the firstborn and would fear it more than anything that had come upon them, and they had already seen all the words of Moses being fulfilled among them; therefore HaShem informed him that He is hardening his heart, in order to multiply His signs upon him through the plague of the firstborn in man and beast, and judgments upon their gods. And Rashi said: the plague of the firstborn, and the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, and drowning the Egyptians within it. But this is not tenable, because it says (Exodus 11:10), \"and he did not send the children of Israel from his land.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:52.619295927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}